WEBVTT

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.970
I missed you

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.350
Howard! Sharla!

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.260
We lost Howard and Sharla to the quicksand...

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.280
...and in the midst of that sadness...

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.610
...crossed the blazing hot desert.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:37.520
What is this?

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:43.780
And finally, we reached the main computer, Survive, which we had been heading for.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:46.670
But...

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:54.430
Mom! Dad!

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:00.730
...Adam's parents had already died.

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:14.980
And then, we were led to this beautiful area by Tako, the robot we met there.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.610
Okay, it's all clear.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:05.750
It's so dangerous with drones here there 'n everywhere.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:09.550
But this is the only place we can come to get food.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.300
Is there no way to stop them from working?

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:16.930
We'd have to do something about the main computer Survive for that.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.770
'N that won't be so easy.

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:29.500
Luna!

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.720
You startled us!

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:34.030
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.280
It's delicious.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:47.650
Was there any danger?

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.160
We were chased by drones, but we made it somehow.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.830
First we have to do somethin' to make contact with Survive.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:58.070
It's a computer that says people aren't necessary, after all.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.650
We have to be careful.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.860
Looks like this might become a drawn-out battle.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:06.360
It's true. For now we should gather as much food and water as we can.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.850
Tako's hungrily awaiting us, too.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.000
He's probably just fast asleep right now.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:19.260
After we've rested a little, let's go collect a little more food.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:22.160
It's like the island here.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:37.370
Cheers!

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.720
Luna... Luna!

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.050
Look!

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:58.490
That's...

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:01.110
It's Pague!

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:02.080
It looks so similar.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:02.980
It's true.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:04.710
Pague!

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:09.250
Adam! It's dangerous!

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:10.460
Be careful!

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:11.720
Leave it to me!

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.330
Pague!

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:22.670
He's a perfect match for Pague.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.130
Although he's teensy.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:31.480
Here.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.380
Do you mind if I call you Pague?

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:49.900
I think that's his mom.

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:01.000
Pague! See you later!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:07.850
Luna! Behind you!

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:47.160
It can't be...

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:53.800
Luna...

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.600
Sharla...

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:56.610
Howard...

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.070
You were alive!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.000
I can't believe it!

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:05.310
Sharla! Sharla!

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:07.000
Howard!

00:08:08.950 --> 00:08:10.210
Were you hurt?

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.610
I missed you.

00:08:12.730 --> 00:08:13.670
Sharla!

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:16.000
Howard!

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:19.470
What a relief! You ain't ghosts!

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:38.830
It's delicious.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.460
We'll get more later.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.820
Hey, how did you guys survive?

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:47.330
You must have gotten out of that sand somehow.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:49.410
I'm just glad you're okay.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:51.500
How did you get all the way here?

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:54.320
Um...

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.340
Everyone, Sharla can't get a word in edgewise.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:08:58.970
Sorry.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.510
Sorry for making you all worry.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:04.300
Nothin' to apologize for.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.380
I thought we were done for back then as well.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:11.810
The sand was pressing down on us, and we couldn't escape.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:17.350
We could hear all your voices, but we couldn't get free from the sand.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:31.180
Howard and I fell into some flowing water under the sand.

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.600
I don't remember anything after that.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.030
When we came to, we were in this forest.

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:42.550
An underground aqueduct?

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:47.890
Come to think of it, it might be connected to the one we came through.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:50.390
Weren't you attacked by the drones?

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:52.820
There's many of them here too.

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:58.750
We were attacked, but Howard made a bow, and used it to get away from them.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:00.810
Howard did?

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:07.110
Well, from the start I figured Howard was the kind that wouldn't die even if you killed 'im.

00:10:16.560 --> 00:10:17.910
What's wrong, Howard?

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:19.710
Yer awful quiet.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.570
Anyways, I'm glad you're all safe too.

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:26.220
It's a relief to be back together.

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:28.930
Lots has happened to us since then too.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:30.130
Lots?

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:33.100
That's right! Howard, here.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:40.370
Your mirror that was in this jacket saved us when it seemed like we were going to be killed.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:41.610
Thanks.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:44.680
Howard?

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.610
What's wrong, Howard?

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:49.410
Are you feeling ill?

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.830
Are you hurt somewhere?

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:53.270
I'll take a look.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.620
It's okay! He's not hurt, he's just a little tired.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:03.060
He hasn't slept much, so once he rests a while, he'll be better.

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:05.980
But I still think you should let her take a look.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:07.750
I'll leave it here, Howard.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.170
Leave him alone for now.

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:14.980
Okay.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:17.050
It was tough, after all.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:20.100
Yeah, take it easy a while.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:21.320
That's for the best.

00:11:21.470 --> 00:11:22.180
I agree.

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.920
Yeah. You'll be back on your feet in no time.

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:30.320
Here.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:35.490
It's your handkerchief, Sharla.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:39.580
Thank you! I guess you held onto it for me.

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:50.840
What's wrong?

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:55.450
Nothing at all.

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:03.900
Today we hafta celebrate them comin' back!

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:05.350
Let's do it!

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:08.050
Now we can all go home to the colony!

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:10.650
We're all back together.

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:13.660
Sharla, Howard, welcome back!

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.280
Welcome back!

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.270
We're back!

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:19.710
Well, back to gathering food.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:23.080
The ones Luna and Kaoru brought back were super delicious.

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:24.280
That's right.

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:06.920
We're back!

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:10.090
Luna, how did things seem in the forest?

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:12.090
It was odd.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:13.220
Over there too?

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:14.760
What'chall talkin' 'bout?

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:17.200
The drones have disappeared.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:18.810
That's pretty weird.

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:21.430
We haven't been attacked at all.

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:23.680
There wasn't even any sign of them.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.660
Well good! Now we can gather food without having to worry.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:28.600
It's true!

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:30.920
I'm more unsettled by the sudden change.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:32.420
I feel the same.

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:36.530
For the drones which had been attacking us all that time to suddenly disappear is...

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.790
Survive's plannin' somethin', you think?

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:46.450
Anyways, we'll be fine when we go back to the hidden area.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:48.880
What's the hidden area?

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.920
A place Adam's parents made.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:55.450
It's the only place Survive's control doesn't reach.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:58.710
It probably hasn't even realized the hidden area exists.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:00.890
To think a place like that existed...

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:04.150
We only come here to get food when we need it.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:08.870
There's a weird maintenance robot in the hidden area named Tako.

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:09.690
Tako?

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:12.940
Although his real name is more difficult.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:15.650
We couldn't figure it out, so we call 'im Tako.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:21.410
Anyways, once we're back in the hidden area, we'll be fine, so Sharla, Howard, rest easy.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.010
Luna, Pague's come back!

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:34.330
Can I go?

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:36.930
Those scary things are gone, right?

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:40.100
But we don't know if it's really safe yet.

00:14:41.050 --> 00:14:41.760
I can't?

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:43.670
Adam, let's go.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.210
But...

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.230
It's okay. Howard will be with us too.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.510
Leave it to us.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.470
Let's go, Adam.

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.910
Sharla, hurry!

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:13.600
Come on, let's go.

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:26.870
It is okay to let him go?

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:32.400
I think finding out his parents are dead is still hard on Adam.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:36.650
He's actin' cheerful so we won't worry.

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:40.820
And because Adam loved Pague...

00:15:43.820 --> 00:15:46.710
Howard and Sharla are with him, so he'll be fine.

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:48.170
I suppose.

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:55.450
Pague, you're a good boy, aren't you?

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:56.350
Adam.

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:07.070
They're so pretty!

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:10.450
I'm sure Luna would be happy if you picked some and brought them back.

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:12.230
I wonder if I can pick them.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.910
I'll help you too.

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.030
Really?

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:18.250
Then I'll go pick some!

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:43.030
I can't go any further because the branch is too narrow.

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:45.300
You're light, Adam, so you can make it.

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:45.570
Luna, help me!

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:48.510
Luna...

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:50.720
What's wrong?

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.710
Adam's calling.

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:54.660
I heard Adam's voice!

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:55.860
What'd you say?

00:17:55.930 --> 00:18:12.310
Luna!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.150
Sharla!

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:16.100
Adam and Howard...

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:20.050
Bell, take care of Howard!

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:20.570
Got it!

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:33.410
Kaoru! Bell!

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.930
Adam!

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:53.650
Adam... Adam...

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:56.060
Adam? Adam!

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:02.650
It's okay.

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:27.550
Adam!

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:33.770
Snap out of it!

00:19:35.010 --> 00:19:36.660
Snap out of it, Adam!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.070
Alright!

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:50.110
They okay?

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:52.930
They're fine.

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:57.920
I wanted to give Luna flowers...

00:19:58.180 --> 00:20:00.370
It's okay! You don't have to say anything!

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:05.910
Should I take a look?

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:16.810
Nothin' outta the ordinary.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:18.250
What a relief.

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:19.310
I'm glad to hear it.

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:22.020
Is Howard okay too?

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:23.720
As you can see.

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:27.850
But he looks a little blue around the gills.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:31.710
Don't tell me he's been infected by the malignant nanos!

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:33.250
Of course not!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:36.810
But I'm concerned about his constant lack of energy.

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:38.200
That's true...

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:41.160
If worst comes to worst and he's been infected by the malignant nanos...

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:45.960
...as long as we have this emitter we could treat it, so there's nothing to worry about.

00:20:47.420 --> 00:20:50.090
Howard, why don't you have Chako take a look?

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.340
That way we won't worry.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:53.870
That's unnecessary.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.120
C'mon, it'll be done in a flash.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:57.660
It's unnecessary!

00:20:58.710 --> 00:21:00.310
Howard, that's dangerous!

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:24.250
You might have noticed about Howard...

00:21:25.670 --> 00:21:31.130
...but when we were buried in the sand, though we survived, I don't think he can forget the terror.

00:21:31.860 --> 00:21:34.820
Even now when I think about it, I quiver in fear.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:41.140
In spite of that, I overcame my fear because of my determination to see you all again...

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:45.360
...but I think it'll take time for Howard.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:48.580
Just leave him alone for a while.

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:49.400
Please?

00:21:50.610 --> 00:21:52.110
Sharla, I'm sorry.

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:56.280
I didn't realize the painful feelings you'd gone through.

00:21:57.320 --> 00:21:58.260
Luna...

00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:12.210
Let's go back.

00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:30.700
It seems like the drones really have disappeared.

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:34.030
What's going on?

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:36.850
This way.

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:07.000
I'm soooo happy Howard and Sharla're alive!

00:23:08.570 --> 00:23:12.810
But I'm worried they're acting a little strangely.

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:18.850
Anyways, we have to shut down Survive as soon as possible and take the space ship.

00:23:18.850 --> 00:23:21.360
Alright! Leave it to me!

00:23:21.660 --> 00:23:23.910
My skills fit the bill! Snip snip snip!

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:27.550
Next time: Let's start!
